B=<repo>; cd "$B"; bd create --title="daemon: the Trusted level's safety argument depends on IMAP being localhost, and nothing verifies it" --type=task --priority=2 --description="internal/daemon/handler.go:155-160 carries an unfiled placeholder:

    // Proton E2E headers are safe when IMAP source is Proton Bridge on
    // localhost -- Bridge controls these headers for internal messages.
    // External SMTP injection of these headers is blocked by Bridge.
    // TODO(beadle-xxx): verify IMAP is localhost as additional guard.

This bead is that TODO ('beadle-xxx' was never assigned an ID).

WHY IT MATTERS: channel.Trusted is one of only two trust levels OnNewMail accepts before creating a mission (handler.go:162). Unlike Verified, which rests on a real GPG signature verified in an isolated keyring, Trusted rests entirely on two headers — X-Pm-Content-Encryption: end-to-end and X-Pm-Origin: internal. Those headers are only trustworthy because Proton Bridge sets them and Bridge is assumed to be on localhost. Nothing checks that assumption.

If the daemon were pointed at a non-Bridge IMAP server, or at a Bridge-like endpoint that is not local, an attacker able to set those two headers would reach the same trust level as a GPG-signed sender. The x-permission check still applies, so this is not a full bypass on its own — it requires an ungranted-to-granted pairing — but it removes the cryptographic basis from one of the two accepted trust levels and replaces it with an unverified environmental assumption.

The comment states the assumption honestly, which is why this is a gap rather than a hidden flaw. What is missing is the enforcement the comment itself calls for.

SCOPE: verify the configured IMAP host resolves to loopback before honoring Proton-origin headers, and refuse to classify a message as Trusted otherwise (falling back to whatever the signature evidence alone supports). Consider whether this belongs in verifyTrust or earlier at config validation, and whether a non-localhost IMAP should downgrade Trusted or refuse to start.

TESTING: the daemon test tier (beadle-gi5t) covers gate 1 with a Proton-trusted message via testenv.BuildTrustedMessage. A negative case is now cheap to add — same builder, non-loopback IMAP host, assert the message is not accepted as Trusted. Verify it fails with the guard removed.

Found while auditing intended-vs-real for the design status artifact." 2>&1 | tail -3
